> Just curious, but this has never happened to me before.  On the
> first level of the mines, I encountered a ghost, with a little
> bit of loot---in sum, what looks like a bones.  But the ghost
> behaves in every way as if it were a pet, although I certainly
> did nothing to tame it; my first real realization that it was
> there, in fact, was the message "you displaced the ghost" (or
> something very similar).  There was a magic trap nearby, which I
> hit just before finding the ghost, but I don't see off hand how
> this could tame it.
>
> Does anyone know what could have caused this, or is it just
> something that happens, with a fair degree of rareness?  (Given
> the number of ghosts I've seen, it would have to be very, very
> rare.)

When a magic trap gives the "You feel charismatic!" message, you gain
1 point of CHA and you tame every tameable monster adjacent to you.

It is not uncommon for a magic trap to blind the player and generate
dangerous monsters which kill the player within a turn or two.  So the
trap is also likely to be the cause of the bones file.


